1kl9|n|A variety of quartz, of a color between grass green and leek green, which is found associated with common chalcedony. It was much esteemed by the ancients for making engraved ornaments. ; The viscous material of an animal or vegetable cell, out of which the various tissues are formed by a process of differentiation; protoplasm. ; Unorganized material; elementary matter. ; A mixture of starch and glycerin, used as a substitute for ointments.	n:1gsg,134,3~1gsg,134,3	N:hsb,146,9~hsb,146,9
