1klu|a|Having the power to give form or fashion to a mass of matter; as, the plastic hand of the Creator. ; Capable of being molded, formed, or modeled, as clay or plaster; -- used also figuratively; as, the plastic mind of a child. ; Pertaining or appropriate to, or characteristic of, molding or modeling; produced by, or appearing as if produced by, molding or modeling; -- said of sculpture and the kindred arts, in distinction from painting and the graphic arts.	j:1ifi,68,11;1w1a,64,6;1pm0,63,4;8x8,61,5;65z,60,9;12l4,59,16;ivv,52,4;1kaq,50,4;1uay,48,2;1w18,47,2;8x3,45,4;1rap,40,3;21im,40,2;7vz,40,1;1hu4,40,3~scq,8,25;1hsu,11,21;1hv0,19,18;12l4,59,16;rak,7,13;19bs,9,12;25xr,26,12;1ifi,68,11;1vps,35,10;1k17,26,10;65z,60,9;6w5,31,8;2a1x,32,6;1w1a,64,6;8x8,61,5	e:1bj5,55,14;16ri,16,18~16ri,16,18;1bj5,55,14
