1kmo|n|A plat; a plan; a sketch; a model; a pattern. Used also figuratively. ; A place laid out after a model. ; Any flat or horizontal surface; especially, one that is raised above some particular level, as a framework of timber or boards horizontally joined so as to form a roof, or a raised floor, or portion of a floor; a landing; a dais; a stage, for speakers, performers, or workmen; a standing place. ; A declaration of the principles upon which a person, a sect, or a party proposes to stand; a declared policy or system; as, the Saybrook platform; a political platform. ; A light deck, usually placed in a section of the hold or over the floor of the magazine. See Orlop.	a:9qv,75,166~9qv,75,166	v:xun,26,3;9qv,21,4;1mxc,5,4~1mxc,5,4;9qv,21,4;xun,26,3	V:w01,30,3;1c7n,27,2;1ucb,23,1~w01,30,3;1c7n,27,2;1ucb,23,1	n:9qy,35,2;1uim,29,5;9qv,11,2;1mx4,11,11;6wc,8,6~1mx4,11,11;6wc,8,6;1uim,29,5;9qv,11,2;9qy,35,2	N:1c7n,33,3;1wlx,30,4;1ucb,23,1;136,15,1;280a,1,4~280a,1,4;1wlx,30,4;1c7n,33,3;136,15,1;1ucb,23,1
